                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Trappola is an early Venetian trick-taking card game that spread through Central Europe and influenced later games including Stovkahra and Coteccio.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Trappola was current in Venice by the early sixteenth century and became popular in Central Europe from the seventeenth through nineteenth centuries; dedicated Trappola card production survived into the twentieth century.',
